      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Experiments on conscious cats have demonstrated cardiovascular responses of two types to nociceptive effects. A reverse correlation between the changes in arterial pressure, heart rate and cardiotropic component of the baroreceptor reflex has been noted. The function of baroreceptor reflexes has been analyzed by the multivariable correlation technique. The role of the above reflexes is discussed in hemodynamic regulation during exposure to nociceptive stress."},
